docs {
  # Redeem Referral Balance
  
  Use this endpoint when the user wants to move referral rewards into their main wallet.
  
  This is not a bank withdrawal. It is like cashback becoming spendable balance inside the app.
  
  ## Endpoint
  
  `POST /api/v1/wallet/referral/redeem`
  
  ## Authentication
  
  Required.
  
  ```txt
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
  ```
  
  ## Body Fields
  
  `amount`  
  Required. Amount to move from referral wallet to main wallet. Minimum is NGN
  30 and it must not exceed `withdrawableReferralBalance` returned by Referral
  Summary.
  
  `transactionPin`  
  Required. User's 4-digit transaction PIN.
  
  ## Expected Success Response
  
  ```json
  {
    "message": "Referral earnings redeemed successfully",
    "wallet": {
      "mainBalance": 6000,
      "referralBalance": 0
    },
    "transactions": [
      {
        "type": "referral_redeem",
        "walletType": "referral",
        "direction": "debit",
        "amount": 1000
      },
      {
        "type": "referral_redeem",
        "walletType": "main",
        "direction": "credit",
        "amount": 1000
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ## Common Errors
  
  Wrong transaction PIN:
  
  ```json
  {
    "message": "Invalid transaction PIN"
  }
  ```
  
  Not enough referral balance:
  
  ```json
  {
    "message": "Insufficient wallet balance"
  }
  ```

  Amount below NGN 30:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "The minimum referral withdrawal is NGN 30."
  }
  ```

  Requested amount includes a locked NGN 300 reward:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "A NGN 300 reward earned from one referred user is locked until that user buys a service worth at least NGN 1000. You can currently redeem NGN 90."
  }
  ```
  
  ## Frontend Notes
  
  Fetch `GET /api/v1/referrals/summary` before displaying the form.

  Show or enable the redeem button when:

  ```txt
  withdrawableReferralBalance >= settings.minimumRedeemAmount
  ```

  Use `withdrawableReferralBalance`, not the total `referralBalance`, as the
  maximum redeemable amount.
  
  Referral earnings are 3% of the first successful deposit, capped at NGN 300
  per referred user. Only a reward that reaches NGN 300 is locked. It unlocks
  after that referred user successfully buys at least NGN 1,000 of services.
  Smaller rewards from different users remain redeemable.
}
